[Music]  we have already seen the characteristics  of images formed by plane mirrors the  image is of the same size as the object  and it's also at the same distance away  from the mirror as the object is and the  image follows left-right reversal it  means that the objects right is the  images left and vice versa and lastly  the image formed by a plane mirror is a  virtual image so what about the image is  formed by concave mirrors do they have  the same characteristics you all must  have seen the reflection of your face in  a spoon spoon has two smooth surfaces  one curved inside and the other curved  outside however it is not perfectly  spherical for ease of understanding we  can consider the reflecting surface  which is curved inwards as a concave  mirror I will show you how the image  appears but using an actual concave  mirror and not a spoon so let's try and  find out the properties of an image  formed by a concave mirror I will show  you two views of the mirror the front  view and the side view the side view is  just to show the different positions  where the object is kept as it's  difficult to do that in the front view  okay so let B be its bowl see it's  center of curvature this line is the  principal axis and the F is the  principal focus also called focal point  assume that initially the object is kept  close to the mirror I will make a table  on the right with three columns telling  us where the object is kept the size of  the image formed and the nature of the  image that is whether the image is  virtual or real so initially the  position of the object is between F and  B what is the size of the image we see  the reflection in the concave mirror and  the image is bigger in size we see that  it's enlarged the dimensions of the  image are greater than the dimensions of  the object so we say that when the  object is between the principal focus  and  the image formed is enlarged also is the  image upright or erect what about the  nature of the image is it real or  virtual yes it's the virtual image it  appears to be formed behind the mirror  where is the location of the image it is  a virtual image so it does not have any  location it only appears to be formed in  a location behind the mirror but we will  find that location in our next video  using ray diagrams for now let's move  the subject away from the mirror and see  how the dimensions and the nature of the  image very relative to the object you  will find that as I move this object  away its image gets even bigger and when  the object is at the principle focus the  image is huge we say that when the  object is at the principle focus the  image is highly enlarged is it a real or  a virtual image it is a real image since  it's a real image it's upside down or we  use the other word for it which is  inverted it is formed on the same side  of the mirror as the object is and  believe it or not the image is actually  formed infinitely far away when I start  moving this object away from the focal  point towards point C the image is still  enlarged but the size is reducing and  what is the nature of this image yes  here as well the image is upside down  it's a real image when the object is at  Point C the image is still real and  inverted  but now the size of the object and its  image is same yes at this point both the  object and the image are of the same  size what next  if I move this object beyond Point C the  image remains real and inverted but now  the size of the image is actually  smaller compared to the size of the  object so we say that the image is  diminished this is also a real image as  the objects keep moving beyond C  the size of the image keeps on reducing  what if the object is placed at infinity  well if you remember that in our  previous video we saw that the rays of  light parallel to each other as well as  to the principal axis will converge at  the focal point and in that example our  object was the Sun Sun is at a very  large distance away from the earth and  hence we consider the rays of light from  it reaching the surface of the earth to  be almost parallel the image of the Sun  will be formed at the principal focus  similarly if any object kept infinitely  far away from the mirror on the  principal axis all the rays from it can  be thought of as traveling parallel to  each other after reflection they will  all converge at the focus and the image  of that infinitely far away object will  be formed at this point yes this is the  point size image it's a highly  diminished image and it's also a real  image take a moment and go through the  properties of images again from this  table you can see that the image is  virtual only when the object is kept  between the focal point and the pole  otherwise the image formed is always a  real image in the next video we will  find out the position of these images  using grade diagrams  [Music]

